-"Let $T>0$, $N\\ge1$, $h=T/N$, $p\\ge1$, and $C_0,C,L\\ge0$. If nonnegative real numbers $e_0,\\ldots,e_N$ satisfy\n$$e_0\\le C_0h^p,\\qquad e_{n+1}\\le(1+Lh)e_n+Ch^{p+1}\\quad(0\\le n<N),$$\nthen, when $L>0$,\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}e_n\\le\\left(C_0\\exp(LT)+C\\frac{\\exp(LT)-1}{L}\\right)h^p,$$\nand, when $L=0$,\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}e_n\\le(C_0+CT)h^p.$$"+"Let $T>0$, $N\\in\\mathbb N$ with $N\\ge1$, $h=T/N>0$, $p\\in\\mathbb R$ with $p\\ge1$, and $C_0,C,L\\ge0$. Real powers of the positive base $h$ are as in [[def-real-power]]. If nonnegative real numbers $e_0,\\ldots,e_N$ satisfy\n$$e_0\\le C_0h^p,\\qquad e_{n+1}\\le(1+Lh)e_n+Ch^{p+1}\\quad(0\\le n<N),$$\nthen, when $L>0$,\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}e_n\\le\\left(C_0\\exp(LT)+C\\frac{\\exp(LT)-1}{L}\\right)h^p,$$\nand, when $L=0$,\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}e_n\\le(C_0+CT)h^p.$$"
